            <ArticleTitle>[The influence of postischemic reperfusion on the recovery of ischemic lesions of the left ventricle (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>321-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In an isolated dog heart preparation the influence of normothermic ischemic arrest and recovery of the ventricular function during the period of post-ischemic reperfusion were investigated. If ischemic arrest has caused a depression of ventricular function, the functional recovery of the myocardium cannot be improved significantly by a prolonged reperfusion of the empty beating heart.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
